  "known_limitations": [
    "illustrated_process is actively unreliable, not just undercounted: human eye-check (2026-08-13) confirmed 7 misclassified pages, all sharing the same layout -- a small process figure/sketch in the margin of a text-dense page. Two (76v, 77r) were wrongly called only_voynese (the process content wasn't registered at all). Five (77v, 78r, 81r, 81v, 83v) were wrongly called circular_diagram=true -- these are NOT circular diagrams, they are illustrated_process pages the model misread as diagrams once it noticed something was there. Net effect: circular_diagram=true entries without an existing catalog tag should NOT be trusted as new-tag candidates without human review -- this run's untagged-candidate sample was 0/5 correct. illustrated_process's true count in this section is very likely several times the raw total below.",
    "circular_diagram spot-checked against the 17 pre-existing catalog Circular diagram tags: 15/17 agreed; the 2 disagreements were both foldout-related (85v_and_86r foldout and a part-crop sibling that slipped past this run's exclusion filter), not model misses. This agreement rate does NOT extend to circular_diagram hits outside the pre-tagged set -- see the illustrated_process note above.",
    "One page (11v.png) returned all four fields false despite notes describing an illustration -- likely a genuine miss, not yet corrected.",
    "One page (72v_(part)_seq131.png) returned a self-contradictory combination (circular_diagram=true AND only_voynese=true) -- only_voynese is defined as no significant illustration, so this pairing is invalid as given; flagged, not corrected."
